<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gao Cheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">521–549</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao">Gao</a> Cheng was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao-huan">Gao Huan</a> and regent of the Eastern Wei after his father's death in 547. He faced the defection of the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hou-jing">Hou Jing</a> to the south and continued the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-wei">Western Wei</a>. He was assassinated by a kitchen slave in 549, and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wenxuan-of-northern-qi">Gao Yang</a> founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-qi">Northern Qi</a> the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gao-cheng.jpg" alt="Gao Cheng" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%B8%96%E5%AD%90%E9%AB%98%E6%BE%84%EF%BC%88%E5%8C%97%E5%8F%B2%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%EF%BC%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
